Z||000000||Philphine||03-24-2001||10:51 PM||||<BR>keeping an eye out for the pieces to try rear brake conversion. the salvation army thrift store car lot near me has an '86 6000ste. i'd have to get the whole car so monday i'm gonna see how much they want for it.<P>they wrote blown head on the window but i'm not really interested in the engine anyway. it dose have rear disc brakes also. can i take advantage of that in any way? what else might i be able to use if i have to get the whole car? it also has the steering wheel radio controls but a note inside the car says the radio dosen't work.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||03-24-2001||11:15 PM||||Off the top of my head, I don't think those had rear disc brakes, but I could be wrong. The steering wheel radio controls uses IR on my Grand Prix. If the radio don't work, the controls still might. Grab another stereo out of a salvage yard from a Pontiac with the radio controls (if has theftlock, you'll need to enter a code before it's removed) or there are some kits for adapting certain aftermarket stereos to factory remote controls. That would be cool in a Fiero. Are you sure those are radio controls and not cruise controls on the steering wheel?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-24-2001||11:28 PM||||According to my info 6000STE rear brake uses the same parts as Fiero. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||03-25-2001||12:09 AM||||yes on both counts batboy. looked inthe window at the stereo controls and throught the back wheel at the brake disc. i wouldn't have noticed if the wheels themselves didn't say disc brakes. even then i kinda though so what, all cars have disc brakes now. but in trying to read it on the wheel i saw the disc.<P>and thanks ogre. if i get it the more parts i can get off it the more worth it it would be.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||03-25-2001||12:48 AM||||STE rear brakes are disc, but single rotor. The calipers are the same as the Fiero's. The bolt pattern is 5 on 115 rather than the Fiero 5 on 100. The rotor won't fit and is single so there is no gain.<P>I have the STE rear discs on my Ciera GT. <BR>TK||||reg||1
