Z||000007||85Josh||03-30-2001||06:27 PM||||Phil, have you checked the local yards to see what they want for these parts? I often have good luck with All State, they will let you pick your own parts. They quoted me $75 to pull the A-arms, front and rear, plus spindles from the lone Fiero they had. I've also heard good things about Amen U-Pick, just never been out there. Let me know if you do this, I'm interested and would be willing to help.<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jay||03-30-2001||06:47 PM||||I have Pontiac 6000 vented rotors on my 86 GT/Northstar.  The difference is in the bolt pattern 5X115 compared to Fiero's 5x100.  If you want to see it on the car there are photos on my website <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> <BR>It may be cheaper as was mentioned to just buy the parts seperate rather than the whole car.  Check it out first especially if you don't have room to store it.||||reg||1
